[2025-09-23 20:34:23,861][heimdall.core][INFO] - Cleaned output : entities:
  - name: GLOVE OBJECTIVE FUNCTION
    type: method
    description: "The mathematical formulation of the GloVe objective function, which is the core of the GloVe method. It is represented as:  ∑i,j f(Xij) (wiT wj + bi + bj - log(Xij))^2, where f is a weighting function, Xij is the co-occurrence count, wi and wj are word embeddings, and bi and bj are bias terms."
  - name: VICO OBJECTIVE FUNCTION
    type: method
    description: "The mathematical formulation of the ViCo objective function. It is represented as:  ∑i,j f(Xij) (wiT wj - log(Xij))^2 + λ ∑i,t ||φt(wi) - bti||^2, where f is a weighting function, Xij is the co-occurrence count, wi and wj are word embeddings, φt is a co-occurrence type-specific transformation function, and bti is a learned bias term."
  - name: WEIGHTING FUNCTION f(X)
    type: method
    description: "The weighting function f(X) used in the GloVe and ViCo objective functions. It assigns lower weight to less frequent, noisy co-occurrences. In the context of the provided text, it is set to the constant 1 for all X in the ViCo method."
  - name: WORD EMBEDDINGS (wi, wj)
    type: method
    description: "The word embeddings, represented as vectors (wi and wj), that the GloVe and ViCo methods learn to represent words in a lower-dimensional space. These embeddings capture semantic relationships between words based on their co-occurrence patterns."
  - name: BIAS TERMS (bi, bj, bti)
    type: method
    description: "The bias terms (bi, bj, and bti) are learnable parameters in the GloVe and ViCo methods. They are used to adjust the dot product of word embeddings and the type-specific transformation to better approximate the log co-occurrence counts."
  - name: CO-OCCURRENCE TYPE-SPECIFIC TRANSFORMATION FUNCTION φt
    type: method
    description: "A function that maps ViCo embeddings to a type-specialized embedding space. This function is used in the ViCo method to capture different types of co-occurrences."

